    "body": "## What\nFix a broken cross-page link in the Jina reranker cookbook page:\n`../DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V3_2.md` → `../DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V3_2`.\n\n## Why\nThe target page is `DeepSeek-V3_2.mdx`, and Mintlify resolves internal links without the file extension. Every other reference to this page (the GLM-5 / 5.1 / 5.2 / 5.3 cookbook pages and `docs.json`) already uses the extensionless form, so this `.md` link was the lone outlier and 404s on the docs site.\n\n## How verified\n- Confirmed the only valid target is `cookbook/autoregressive/DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V3_2.mdx`, and every other in-repo reference uses the extensionless path.\n- `mint broken-links` is the same check SGLang CI runs; this PR's CI exercises it.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38240324060](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38240324060)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38240323690](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38240323690)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
